30,2,,status,Takumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,The taster forms are clear. Nine out of fourteen said they wouldn't commit to a whole year at once.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The treasurer's logs are brutal. Chasing individual payments took six hours a month. A yearly collection took one.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,The sign-in sheets show a quarter of members do two-thirds of the work. Eighteen people never signed in.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,The winter social feedback confirms it. Quiet members feel uneasy about the cost per visit.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Takumi,,The ledger shows seventy percent of costs are fixed. Hall hire and insurance don't care if anyone comes.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, if we charge per event, the admin load will explode.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, yes. That is why I am against activity-based charging. It is unsustainable for the treasurer.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Takumi, if costs are fixed, a flat fee makes sense. But what about the eighteen who never come?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Jonathan, they pay for the privilege of belonging, even if they don't use it.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Shunichi, but the bank statements show a third of renewals needed reminders. People struggle with big upfront sums.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"We need a middle ground. A base fee covers the fixed costs, but we need to be careful with extras.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"A tiered system might work. A low base fee for everyone, and higher tiers for those who use more.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,But the minute books from the named-grade years show friction. People stopped putting themselves forward.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Jonathan, that is a risk. But the current system is failing the quiet members.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"I agree with Benjamin. We need to reduce the admin burden. A flat fee is simplest, but maybe too rigid.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"Let's look at the options. We have to balance fairness, admin load, and accessibility.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"Option B, Tiered Membership, seems the most logical. It allows choice without excessive admin.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I am worried about the social friction, but the data supports a tiered approach.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,I can live with it if the lower tier is genuinely accessible.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Takumi,,I will support it if it simplifies the collection process.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Takumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
