58,3,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Option A is flat. Option B is tiered. Option C is activity-based. C is out due to admin load.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Agreed. C is a nightmare for the treasurer. It is between A and B.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"A is simple, but it punishes the non-attenders. B gives them a choice.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"B allows the quiet members to pay less if they participate less, which addresses their unease.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"B also allows us to set a base fee that covers the fixed costs, which is what the ledger shows we need.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,The taster forms show people don't want a whole year commitment. B offers a lower entry point.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"And the lower tier can be a simple annual payment, reducing the chasing of individual events.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"The friction from the named-grade years is a concern, but we can design the tiers to be less hierarchical.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"Yes, make them about participation level, not status. That should reduce the social pressure.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Takumi,,I am convinced. B is the most robust option given the data.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I vote for B. It balances the concerns of all parties.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,I vote for B. It is the most logical and sustainable.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I vote for B. It addresses the inequality in attendance.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,I vote for B. It respects the quiet members' hesitation.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Takumi,,I vote for B. It simplifies the financial management.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,Unanimous. Let's proceed with the tiered structure.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I will draft the tiers based on the fixed costs.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,I will help define the participation levels.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,I will ensure the language is inclusive.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Takumi,,I will check the bank statements to set the base fee accurately.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
